\bibitem{Thomson_2025}
\BIBentryALTinterwordspacing
A.~Thomson, ``'wall of water': How sprinklers are saving homes from wildfires,'' Oct 2025. [Online]. Available: \url{https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/nova-scotia/how-sprinklers-are-saving-homes-from-wildfires-9.6942238}
\BIBentrySTDinterwordspacing
 \begin{quotation}\noindent This article discusses the use of designated sprinkler systems to protect communities from wildfires in Nova Scotia. This article is current, being published by CBC News in October 2025. The article discusses the use of specialized sprinkler systems, which are a method of fire protection and mitigation in WUI communities and as such provides relevant information on current mitigation strategies. It mentions specifically, the effectiveness of the system in combating the Lake George and Long Lake wildfires, as well as the time and resources required to set up and maintain the system. The article is sufficiently reliable as it comes from a national news network and contains statements from specialists and witnesses to the events of the fires. While the sprinklers were shown to be effective here, the use of these systems in a wider range of scenarios is in dispute due to lack of fire test standards, variation of effectiveness in various conditions, and intense use of resources, which limits the accuracy of the provided information (see reference [29] in the RFP). In addition to describing the use of these sprinkler systems, the article also notes the province’s intention to purchase additional systems based upon their effectiveness. \end{quotation}

